\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just a question, does anyone know the true generation of Lambach Ruthven?<br /> <br /> Emmm, to be honest I think EVERY Meths and \u201cAntes\u201d should be given more canon, they are all very important and filled with mysteries...<br /> <br /> my view:<br /> Loutius, that 4th generation<br /> Nictukus<br /> ...</div> </div> </div> </div>I tend to disagree a bit as if you give a personality to most Antediluvians, you demystify them. How could you even portray an Intelligence 10 creature?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-30T20:53:47-07:00","id":1328446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1326793-so-which-npc-would-you-like-to-get-more-canon-info-on?p=1328437#post1328437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I tend to disagree a bit as if you give a personality to most Antediluvians, you demystify them. How could you even portray an Intelligence 10 creature?</div> </div> </div> </div>With great difficulty.<br /> But Warhammer 40K has had whole novels (admittedly of varying quality) written from the viewpoint of the Primarchs and the setting has not lost its popularity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23725-hardestadttheevenyounger","name":"HardestadtTheEvenYounger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23725_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-30T22:36:02-07:00","id":1328459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1326793-so-which-npc-would-you-like-to-get-more-canon-info-on?p=1328431#post1328431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just a question, does anyone know the true generation of Lambach Ruthven?<br /> <br /> Emmm, to be honest I think EVERY Meths and \u201cAntes\u201d should be given more canon, they are all very important and filled with mysteries...<br /> <br /> my view:<br /> Loutius, that 4th generation<br /> Nictukus<br /> ...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> He was 5th in 2nd ed, then retconned as 4th in revised and Dark Ages revised. V20 gives the view of what Beckett now of the fiend which the known story is that everyone thinks that Dracula diablerized his 4th generation sire Tabak, but that apparently is a ruse, since Tabak was shown as Damek Ruthven's childe, making Tabak a 6th generation vampire (both sources of Dark Ages novel Tzimisce and BJD chapter of Azhi Dahaka are written by Myranda Kalis). I personally keep Lambach lineage from the Dark Ages novel as being 4th, progenitor of the Ruthven lineage and keeper of the clan archives in Samizegetuza, which is also the resting place of the Antediluvian after its destruction by Samiel in the mid 7th century AD.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-30T22:36:02-07:00","id":1328460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1326793-so-which-npc-would-you-like-to-get-more-canon-info-on?p=1328431#post1328431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just a question, does anyone know the true generation of Lambach Ruthven?<br /> <br /> Emmm, to be honest I think EVERY Meths and \u201cAntes\u201d should be given more canon, they are all very important and filled with mysteries...<br /> <br /> my view:<br /> Loutius, that 4th generation<br /> Nictukus<br /> ...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> He was 5th in 2nd ed, then retconned as 4th in revised and Dark Ages revised. V20 gives the view of what Beckett himself knows of the fiend, the story that everyone thinks that Dracula diablerized his 4th generation sire Tabak, but that apparently is a ruse, since Tabak was shown as Damek Ruthven's childe, making Tabak a 6th generation vampire (both sources of Dark Ages novel Tzimisce and BJD chapter of Azhi Dahaka are written by Myranda Kalis). I personally keep Lambach lineage from the Dark Ages novel as being 4th, progenitor of the Ruthven lineage and keeper of the clan archives in Samizegetuza, which is also the resting place of the Antediluvian after its destruction by Samiel in the mid 7th century AD.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1594,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","user":"Saga","date":". 07-31-2019, 04:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-31T03:49:08-07:00","id":1328485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1326793-so-which-npc-would-you-like-to-get-more-canon-info-on?p=1328437#post1328437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I tend to disagree a bit as if you give a personality to most Antediluvians, you demystify them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I say give more &quot;canon&quot;, which means more feats and so on about them. In my opinion it doesn't mean personality.<br /> <br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1326793-so-which-npc-would-you-like-to-get-more-canon-info-on?p=1328437#post1328437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How could you even portray an Intelligence 10 creature?</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span></span></div><br /> <br /> Why not? Canon even has some examples (Yeah, the Unnamed, that Ante-level mage, of course he is a Gary Sue but that's ok.)<br /> <br /> Furthermore, I don't think Antes are so-called Plot Device in Gehenna, they're very powerful but still killable and beatable. I think what authorities want to say is that they're so powerful that you can regard them as Plot, but you can still give them stats if you really want to.<br /> <br /> And even in Gehenna, Antes aren't ultimate badass who have all Lv.10 Disciplines. Most of them may just have 1-3s.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","user":"Rock113","date":". 07-31-2019, 10:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-31T08:08:27-07:00","id":1328528,"title":"","content":"In the grand scheme, he's not that big as many listed here, but I'd appreciate to learn more about that grudge holding bastard Francis Milliner. I think a man that can go toe to toe with the Kennedy clan, get noticed and promoted w/ the Giovanni Clan, and get to the point of succeeding so much that the Family in Venice puts roadblocks in his way(all with 80 years) is a man I want to know more about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24591-sparkeyg","name":"SparkeyG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-09T19:21:32-07:00","id":1330189,"title":"","content":"I\u2019d love for the Nosferatu Warren that dug too deep and became a Wyrm cult, radioactive balefire and all, in the original Clanbook Nosferatu to make a comeback.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11599,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","user":"Reasor","date":". 08-09-2019, 10:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-25T07:19:03-07:00","id":1398777,"title":"","content":"The WH from the Letters in the rulebook.<br /> Brujah and Troille<br /> Johanna Anna von Purgstall","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":26160,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","user":"Koronus","date":". 06-25-2020, 12:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-25T09:19:46-07:00","id":1398799,"title":"","content":"Vestgeir, the Ravnos with the Scandinavian name. Troile. Osiris/Khetamon. Nergal and Rayzeel, did Saulot actually embrace two separate singer slaves? All the really ancient things. The Stoneman. Lasombra. The really old things fascinate me, like the new stuff that just came out about the Atlantic Megalith Builders.<br /> <br /> Anyway, to me it seems really clear that Haquim embraced Ur-Shulgi, and that Ur-Shulgi has been or was Baali for quite some time. Haquim is the Antediluvian with all the powers related to blood, and who embraces a new bloodline with new clan disciplines on a whim. It seems quite possible that he did some kind of his own version of the re-embrace, or suppressed/embraced the Baali re-embrace.<br /> <br /> Personally, I find it hard to swallow that the pre-Muslim more erudite kindered did not know of the Assamite Bloodlines, But I can easily buy that it was a tidbit of information not widely known and that it passed out of the knowledge-base of Kindred embraced after the fall of Byzantium.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2471-trollroot","name":"Trollroot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}